WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.300
CHARLES NESSON: The grand jury is dis-empowered.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.990
And in that sense, the citizenry of We the People

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:29.010
is dis-empowered, when prosecution becomes professionalized,

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:38.400
when it's institutionalized and becomes like a paid government function,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:45.190
in the sense of organization, in 1870 in our history,

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:51.410
the adoption of a professional structure of prosecution.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:57.770
And that, effectively, meant that the grand jury had a staff.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:01.710
And that staff was the prosecution.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:07.930
And the staff eventually takes over the function of the grand jury to a point

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:15.600
where it's no longer any hedge against State power at all.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.810
It's a joke now.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:23.560
On the petit jury side, a two-step process.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:33.850
It's the judges, on the petit jury side, who first took unto themselves

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.390
the sovereignty of the People.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:45.410
They assert that the law, as they see it, is the sovereign.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:51.800
And the jury's job becomes only to apply the law as given to them.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.040
But that was not the original idea.

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:59.320
And then they approve the prosecution.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.920
And they permit plea bargaining, with the result

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:11.000
now that jury trial is more or less a joke, both on the grand jury

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.120
side and the petit jury side.

